<title>BAHRAIN: United Gulf Bank 96 net income edges up.</title>
<headline>United Gulf Bank 96 net income edges up.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>			   (million U.S. dollars, rounded)</p>
<p>    Net income			 15.8   vs   15.6</p>
<p>    Share of associates' income   3.7   vs   nil</p>
<p>    Investment income		14.7   vs   34.0</p>
<p>    Interest income		  14.0   vs    8.6</p>
<p>    Interest expense		 10.4   vs   14.3</p>
<p>    Total dividend		   13.0   vs   12.0</p>
<p>    Customer deposits		31.2   vs   43.9</p>
<p>    Shareholders' funds	   222.4   vs  221.5</p>
<p>    Assets			    349.8   vs  373.4</p>
<p>Full Name: United Gulf Bank E.C.</p>
<p>Note - The Bahrain-based offshore investment bank is 97 percent owned by Kuwait Investment Projects Company.</p>
</text>
